      <h1 id="hcp-override-resource-util" class="group scroll-mt-20">Overriding resource utilization measurements<a href="#hcp-override-resource-util" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>The set of baseline measurements for resource utilization can vary in each hosted cluster. Ensure that you understand the resource utilization needed for your deployment.</p>
      <h2 id="hcp-override_hcp-override-resource-util" class="group scroll-mt-20">Overriding resource utilization measurements for a hosted cluster<a href="#hcp-override_hcp-override-resource-util" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can override resource utilization measurements based on the type and pace of your cluster workload.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create the <code>ConfigMap</code> resource by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <your-config-map-file.yaml>"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Replace <code>&lt;your-config-map-file.yaml&gt;</code> with the name of your YAML file that contains your <code>hcp-sizing-baseline</code> config map.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Create the <code>hcp-sizing-baseline</code> config map in the <code>local-cluster</code> namespace to specify the measurements you want to override. Your config map might resemble the following YAML file:
      <CodeBlock code={"kind: ConfigMap\napiVersion: v1\nmetadata:\n  name: hcp-sizing-baseline\n  namespace: local-cluster\ndata:\n  incrementalCPUUsagePer1KQPS: \"9.0\"\n  memoryRequestPerHCP: \"18\"\n  minimumQPSPerHCP: \"50.0\""} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Delete the <code>hypershift-addon-agent</code> deployment to restart the <code>hypershift-addon-agent</code> pod by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc delete deployment hypershift-addon-agent \\\n  -n open-cluster-management-agent-addon"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Observe the <code>hypershift-addon-agent</code> pod logs. Verify that the overridden measurements are updated in the config map by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc logs hypershift-addon-agent -n open-cluster-management-agent-addon"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>Your logs might resemble the following output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"2024-01-05T19:41:05.392Z\tINFO\tagent.agent-reconciler\tagent/agent.go:793\tsetting cpuRequestPerHCP to 5\n2024-01-05T19:41:05.392Z\tINFO\tagent.agent-reconciler\tagent/agent.go:802\tsetting memoryRequestPerHCP to 18\n2024-01-05T19:53:54.070Z\tINFO\tagent.agent-reconciler\tagent/hcp_capacity_calculation.go:141\tThe worker nodes have 12.000000 vCPUs\n2024-01-05T19:53:54.070Z\tINFO\tagent.agent-reconciler\tagent/hcp_capacity_calculation.go:142\tThe worker nodes have 49.173369 GB memory"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <p>If the overridden measurements are not updated properly in the <code>hcp-sizing-baseline</code> config map, you might see the following error message in the <code>hypershift-addon-agent</code> pod logs:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"2024-01-05T19:53:54.052Z\tERROR\tagent.agent-reconciler\tagent/agent.go:788\tfailed to get configmap from the hub. Setting the HCP sizing baseline with default values.\t{\"error\": \"configmaps \\\"hcp-sizing-baseline\\\" not found\"}"} lang="terminal" title="Example error" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="hcp-disable-metrics_hcp-override-resource-util" class="group scroll-mt-20">Disabling the metric service monitoring<a href="#hcp-disable-metrics_hcp-override-resource-util" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">After you enable the <code>hypershift-addon</code> managed cluster add-on, metric service monitoring is configured by default so that OpenShift Container Platform monitoring can gather metrics from <code>hypershift-addon</code>. If needed, you can disable metric service monitoring.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Log in to your hub cluster by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc login"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Edit the <code>hypershift-addon-deploy-config</code> add-on deployment configuration specification by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc edit addondeploymentconfig hypershift-addon-deploy-config \\\n  -n multicluster-engine"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Add the <code>disableMetrics=true</code> customized variable to the specification, as shown in the following example:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: addon.open-cluster-management.io/v1alpha1\nkind: AddOnDeploymentConfig\nmetadata:\n  name: hypershift-addon-deploy-config\n  namespace: multicluster-engine\nspec:\n  customizedVariables:\n  - name: hcMaxNumber\n    value: \"80\"\n  - name: hcThresholdNumber\n    value: \"60\"\n  - name: disableMetrics\n    value: \"true\""} lang="yaml" />
      <p>The <code>disableMetrics=true</code> customized variable disables metric service monitoring for both new and existing <code>hypershift-addon</code> managed cluster add-ons.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the changes to the configuration specification by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f <filename>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
